      "text": [
        " إِنَّ رَسُولَ اَللَّهِ صَلَّى اَللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَ آلِهِ قَالَ : \"مَا مِنْ نَفَقَةٍ أَحَبَّ إِلَى اَللَّهِ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ مِنْ نَفَقَةِ قَصْدٍ وَ يُبْغِضُ اَلْإِسْرَافَ إِلاَّ فِي اَلْحَجِّ وَ اَلْعُمْرَةِ فَرَحِمَ اَللَّهُ مُؤْمِناً كَسَبَ طَيِّباً وَ أَنْفَقَ مِنْ قَصْدٍ أَوْ قَدَّمَ فَضْلاً \"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.3621 - Ibn Abi Ya'fur narrated from Abu Abdullah (as) that he said:\n\"The Messenger of Allah (swt) (peace be upon him and his family) said:\n'There is no spending more beloved to Allah (swt), the Mighty and Majestic, than moderate spending. He (swt) dislikes extravagance, except in Hajj and Umrah.\nMay Allah (swt) have mercy on a believer who earns lawfully, spends moderately, or gives something in charity from his surplus.' \""
        ]
      }
    },
